  "notes": "{静|しず}める is a transitive verb meaning to calm or quiet something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {静|しず}める (transitive, ichidan): to calm something\n- {静|しず}まる (intransitive, godan): to become calm\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {心|こころ}を{静|しず}める (to calm one's mind)\n- {怒|いか}りを{静|しず}める (to calm one's anger)\n- {気持|きも}ちを{静|しず}める (to calm one's feelings)\n- {騒|さわ}ぎを{静|しず}める (to quiet a commotion)\n\nWRITING:\n- Usually written with {静|しず}める (quiet, calm)\n- Not to be confused with {鎮|しず}める, which emphasizes suppression by force and is more common for sense 2 in formal writing",
